From cda63ff2a20ce05538ef93d63beddc86b5e5450f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:39:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] feat(mcp): return short receipts from writes and
 deletes

Insight, dashboard, annotation, survey, cohort and action writes echoed
the whole object: every tile's query, compiled HogQL, cached results and
two full user objects. On the friction session 73 writes and deletes
returned 61,363 tokens, of which 4,187 were needed.

A tool with `response.receipt` in tools.yaml now returns its identity
fields (id, short_id, key, name, version when present), the extra fields
it lists, the soft-delete field it set, and `_posthogUrl`. An update
(PATCH or PUT with a body) also reads the object first and lists each
sent field it changed as `changed.<path>: {from, to}` (by index inside
same-length arrays) and each it left alone under `unchanged`. The read
is display-only: the write is the same request as before, so no new
lost-update window opens; `from` can be stale if someone else edits the
object between the read and the write. A failed read falls back to the
stored values. Codegen adds an optional `full` param on these tools that
returns the old response with include/exclude applied.

Receipts are declared on insight-create/update/delete,
dashboard-create/delete/reorder-tiles (tile ids, order and layouts),
annotation-create/annotations-partial-update/annotation-delete,
survey-create/update/delete, cohorts-create/partial-update and
action-create/update/delete.

The text the model reads also shrinks every created_by,
last_modified_by and updated_by user object to {id, name}, in
formatResponse; JSON output and the structured payload keep the full
object.

The generated handlers are edited to match what the generator now
emits, because codegen needs the backend OpenAPI schema.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
